{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q(\\sqrt{3},\\,\\frac{11}{2},\\,-7)$ and parallel to $v=⟨1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-35960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=q+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$ \n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $Q$ is $q=⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,\\frac{11}{2},\\,-7⟩.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,\\frac{11}{2},\\,-7⟩+t⟨1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-35960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-35960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-35960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩+t⟨-7