rset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,1,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,1,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩)-⟨3,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,t,\\,3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{14},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |⟨2t,\\,t,\\,3t⟩| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+(3t)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{14{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{14} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,1,-1⟩+1⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨5,2,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,1,-1⟩-1⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,0,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(5,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,0,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-22291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-22291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-22291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${A}_{1}(2,5,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(0,1,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(4,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,0,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(5,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,0,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(5,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,-1,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(5,3,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,0,4)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-22291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(5,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,0,-4)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-6,2,-1)$ and $Q(-8,0,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(-1)+(-2)+1=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-1,1,3)$ and $Q(0,6,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i+(5t+1)\\,j+b\\,k,\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(6\\,j-k)-(-i+j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =i+5\\,j-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(-i+j+3\\,k)+t(i+5\\,j-4\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(-i+j+3\\,k)+t(i+5\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =(t-1)\\,i+(5t+1)\\,j+(3-4t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(t-1)+(3-4t)+0=2-3t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-162177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0