ave\n\n$$\na+b+c=(2t+4)+(2t+3)+1=4t+8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-162184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5t"] ["math" "1-5t"] ["math" "4t+8"] ["math" "4t-7"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t+8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,2,-1)$ and $Q(0,1,-3).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i+b\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(j-3\\,k)-(3\\,i+2\\,j-k) \\\\  & =-3\\,i-j-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =(3-3t)\\,i+(2-t)\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(3-3t)+(2-t)+1=6-4t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2t-1"] ["math" "3t"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6-4t"] ["math" "t+5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-4t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(5,0,4)$ and $Q(-3,1,5).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ a \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+1+1=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "33723098ec9036a058d34148050980f29b6e83d0e42fe99ed96394043cf200f6"} {"question" "e-12442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(3,-1,7)$ and parallel to $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12442.json" "file_sha256" "6eba162d9ec842559fc59d21a932fb6cad66718ce22958568b1da467095c79a8"} {"question" "e-12442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12442.json" "file_sha256" "6eba162d9ec842559fc59d21a932fb6cad66718ce22958568b1da467095c79a8"} {"question" "e-12443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12443.json" "file_sha256" "d6bd5a2a20062619227cdbeff6869d6df126f1c578baf04e2cafc5d561d3b44f"} {"question" "e-12443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,2,7⟩-⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12443.json" "file_sha256" "d6bd5a2a20062619227cdbeff6869d6df126f1c578baf04e2cafc5d561d3b44f"} {"question" "e-12444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,2,0)$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}= \\langle -4,1,1 \\rangle.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=6\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12444.json" "file_sha256" "6062ec4fbb2f176a2740b761469e35404432e7bc25608ba488a8f8425503035b"} {"question" "e-12444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\langle 1, 2, 0 \\rangle + t \\langle -4, 1, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩)-⟨1,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=6\\sqrt{2},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-4t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{18{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\pm 3t\\sqrt{2} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ t & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 2$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨1,2,0⟩+2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨-7,4,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨1,2,0⟩-2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨9,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are $A_1(-7, 4, 2)$ and $A_2(9, 0, -2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12444.json" "file_sha256" "6062ec4fbb2f176a2740b761469e35404432e7bc25608ba488a8f8425503035b"} {"question" "e-12445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Using $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j},\\mathbf{k}$ notation, find a parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(-4,1,2)$ and $Q(-2,5,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12445.json" "file_sha256" "0826fc070b78e29e99e9b38ff758f8b19f21082b23ef4d723eb27cf1dc427db4"} {"question" "e-12445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(-2\\,i+5\\,j-k)-(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{r} = (-4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}) + t (2 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{j} - 3 \\, \\mathbf{k})\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k)+t(2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t-4)\\,i+(4t+1)\\,j+(2-3t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/example-12445.json" "fil